                    insight_becoming:       `Becoming a leader: Roche held a provisional leadership identity under public threat, recovered confidence toward the 71% norm, and built a stance grounded in a sustainable purpose. She did identity work, not slide work — and the watching organisation granted her the leadership it was testing.`,
                    insight_armour:         `Confidence rose, but on shallow ground. The recovery looks like authority more than identity — the next setback will test whether anything underneath actually holds. Performed certainty is borrowed, not built.`,
                    insight_fragile:        `Performed authority: Roche projected certainty the room could see through, or chased numbers without a self underneath. Sustainability is low — the chair still feels borrowed, and the next interruption will reopen the same wound.`,
                    insight_partial:        `A partial recovery: some progress, but the identity isn't yet integrated or the stance isn't yet sustainable. The provisional self hasn't been claimed and granted firmly enough to hold under the next threat.`,
                    insight_slogan:         `Sustainability stayed low. A leadership identity that can't survive a second public setback isn't held — it's performed. The purpose needs to be specific enough to lead by and honest enough to hold.`,
                    insight_lowidentity:    `Identity integration is weak: Roche kept clutching the proven expert self instead of claiming the provisional leader self. Transitions destabilise precisely because the old identity no longer fits.`,
                    insight_solo:           `Roche went it alone. Leaders are held into their identity by the right few relationships — solo heroics under threat is isolation dressed as strength, and it rarely sustains.`,
                    insight_leadgone:       `A second team lead left during the crisis — a visible signal to the division that the new leadership wasn't holding. Confidence carried that cost forward.`,
                    insight_held:           `Genuine held leadership: confidence, identity, credibility and a sustainable purpose moving together — authentic <em>and</em> steady, the integration the transition was demanding.`,

                    hint_confidence:        `Team confidence is critically low. Stop polishing the roadmap and address the identity threat directly — owning the miss with a held stance is what moves the 38%.`,
                    hint_sustain:           `The stance isn't sustainable. A purpose or posture that can't survive a second setback is performed, not held — make it specific and honest enough to lead by.`,
                    hint_identity:          `Identity integration is slipping. Roche is clutching the expert self. Claim the provisional leader self and let the right relationships hold it.`,
                    hint_solo:              `Roche is white-knuckling this alone. Choose one or two developmental relationships to be held by — isolation under threat undermines the identity you're building.`,
                    hint_strong:            `Strong balance — confidence, identity and sustainability all healthy. Now anchor it to a specific purpose so it survives the next interruption.`,

